adjudication.rationale:
In EventManager.createAllCalendarEvents, the legacy path for a destination without credentialId is now executed inside the per-destination loop:

```ts
} else {
  const destinationCalendarCredentials = this.calendarCredentials.filter(
    (c) => c.type === destination.integration
  );
  createdEvents = createdEvents.concat(
    await Promise.all(destinationCalendarCredentials.map(async (c) => await createEvent(c, event)))
  );
}
```

This calls `createEvent(c, event)` without the new `externalId` argument, so the returned `EventResult` will have `externalId: undefined` (CalendarManager now returns `{ externalId, credentialId }`). Separately, GoogleCalendarService.createEvent now selects the calendar by matching `cal.credentialId === credentialId`; if the destination entries don’t have credentialId (the legacy case), the `.find(...)` returns undefined and it falls back to `"primary"`, ignoring any configured externalId present on the destination.

Also, because this else-branch runs once per destination, if multiple destinations share the same `integration` type, it will re-create events for the same set of credentials multiple times, causing duplicates.
